{"name":"Red Riding Hood","hex":"#fe2713","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"riding","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of ride"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A path cut through woodland.","The act of one who rides; a mounted excursion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riding"},{"term":"hood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covering for the head, usually attached to a larger garment such as a jacket or cloak.\n A head covering placed on falcons to inhibit their vision.\n A head and neck covering placed on horses to protect against insects and sunlight, to slow coat growth and for warmth.","A head covering placed on falcons to inhibit their vision."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover (something) with a hood.","To extend out from (something), in the manner of a hood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Riding Hood (2011 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Riding Hood is a 2011 American romantic fantasy horror film directed by Catherine Hardwicke, and produced by Leonardo DiCaprio, from a screenplay by David Leslie Johnson. The film is very loosely based on the folk tale \"Little Red Riding Hood\" collected by both Charles Perrault under the name Le Petit Chaperon Rouge and several decades later by the Brothers Grimm as Rotkäppchen. It stars Amanda Seyfried as the title role, with Gary Oldman, Billy Burke, Shiloh Fernandez, Max Irons, Virginia Madsen, Lukas Haas and Julie Christie in supporting roles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Red_riding_hood_ver2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Riding_Hood_(2011_film)","wikidata":"Q815608"},{"title":"Red Riding Hood (1987 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Riding Hood is a 1987 American/Israeli fantasy film by Golan-Globus based on the fairy tale of the same name and part of the film series Cannon Movie Tales."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Red_Riding_Hood_FilmPoster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Riding_Hood_(1987_film)","wikidata":"Q3397699"},{"title":"Little Red Riding Hood","blocks":[{"text":"Little Red Riding Hood is a fairy tale about a young girl and a Big Bad Wolf. Some later versions include a woodsman. Its origins can be traced back to several pre-17th-century European folk tales, with parallels in ancient oral narratives and motifs; it was first recorded in literary form in French by Charles Perrault, and later retold in the 19th-century by the Brothers Grimm."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Little_Red_Riding_Hood_-_J._W._Smith.jpg/330px-Little_Red_Riding_Hood_-_J._W._Smith.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Red_Riding_Hood","wikidata":"Q11838"},{"title":"Red Riding","blocks":[{"text":"Red Riding is a British crime drama limited series written by Tony Grisoni and based on the book series of the same name by David Peace. The series comprises the novels Nineteen Seventy-Four (1999), Nineteen Seventy-Seven (2000), Nineteen Eighty (2001) and Nineteen Eighty-Three (2002), and the first, third, and fourth of these novels became three feature-length television episodes, Red Riding 1974, Red Riding 1980 and Red Riding 1983. They aired in the United Kingdom on Channel 4 beginning on 5 March 2009. The three episodes were released theatrically in the United States between 5 and 11 February 2010, by IFC Films."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/95/Red_Riding_trilogy_%282009%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Riding","wikidata":"Q1819119"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Little_Red_Riding_Hood_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_19993.jpg/500px-Little_Red_Riding_Hood_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_19993.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Little_Red_Riding_Hood_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_19993.jpg/500px-Little_Red_Riding_Hood_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_19993.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Little Red Riding Hood\" as illustrated in a 1927 story anthology","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALittle_Red_Riding_Hood_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_19993.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Little_Red_Riding_Hood_%28136547330%29.jpg/500px-Little_Red_Riding_Hood_%28136547330%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Little_Red_Riding_Hood_%28136547330%29.jpg/1280px-Little_Red_Riding_Hood_%28136547330%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Little_Red_Riding_Hood_%28136547330%29.jpg/500px-Little_Red_Riding_Hood_%28136547330%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gustave Doré's engraving of the scene \"She was astonished to see how her grandmother looked.\"","link":"http